1
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:08,500
Why not carry on her good work?

2
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,540
I enjoyed English, biology and chemistry at school.

3
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:17,280
But which one should I choose to study at university?

4
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:22,900
I did not know the answer until one evening when I sat down at the computer

5
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:25,940
to do some research on great women of China.

6
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:31,820
By chance I came across an article about a doctor called Lin Qiaozhi,

7
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,200
a specialist in women’s diseases.

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:38,520
She lived from 1901 to 1983.

9
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:50,400
One of them caught my eye.

10
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:55,560
It was a small book explaining how to cut the death rate from having

11
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:57,060
and caring for babies.

12
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:02,640
She gave some simple rules to follow for keeping babies clean,

13
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:05,020
healthy and free from sickness.

14
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,380
Why did she write that?

15
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:12,040
Who were the women that Lin Qiaozhi thought needed this advice?

16
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:17,500
I looked carefully at the text and realized that it was intended

17
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,220
for women in the countryside.

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,720
Perhaps if they had an emergency they could not reach a doctor.

19
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:31,480
Suddenly it hit me how difficult it was for a woman to get medical training at

20
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:32,050
that time.

21
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:38,960
That was a generation when girls’ education was always placed second to boys’.

22
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:43,250
Was she so much cleverer than anyone else?

23
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:51,140
Further reading made me realize that it was hard work and determination as well as her gentle nature

24
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:53,380
that got her into medical school.

25
00:01:54,120 --> 00:02:01,020
What made her succeed later on was the kindness and consideration she showed to all her patients.

26
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:05,240
There was story after story of how Lin Qiaozhi,

27
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:10,600
tired after a day’s work, went late at night to deliver a baby

28
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,740
for a poor family who could not pay her.

29
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:18,240
By now I could not wait to find out more about her.

30
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:23,920
I discovered that Lin Qiaozhi had devoted her whole life to her patients

31
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:27,180
and had chosen not to have a family of her own.

32
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:33,680
Instead she made sure that about 50,000 babies were safely delivered.

33
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:37,060
By this time I was very excited.

34
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:43,240
Why not study at medical college like Lin Qiaozhi and carry on her good work?

35
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:47,720
It was still not too late for me to improve my studies,

36
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:51,480
prepare for the university entrance examinations,

37
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,180
and….
